.TH PLENUM 1 "November 2026" "Plenum" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
plenum \- git client CLI for parallel lanes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B plenum
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ path ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Plenum's command-line interface for lane doctor, status, create/remove, start/stop/test, and the local MCP server. The desktop app writes this CLI to
.I ~/.plenum/bin/plenum
on launch.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B doctor [path]
Scan the repo and propose a lane manifest.
.TP
.B status [path]
Print the board (protected, lanes, worktrees).
.TP
.B up <lane> [--force]
Start the lane run command under the supervisor.
.TP
.B down <lane>
Stop the lane processes.
.TP
.B test <lane>
Run the lane test command.
.TP
.B create <name>
Create a feature lane (worktree + setup).
.TP
.B remove <lane> [--force]
Remove a lane worktree.
.TP
.B mcp
Start the local MCP server on stdio.
.TP
.B help
Show usage (same as
.B \-h
/
.BR \-\-help ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print JSON instead of human text.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Skip the drift gate on
.BR up ;
allow
.B remove
when the lane is not safe.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage.
.SH SEE ALSO
.B plenum \-\-help
